Z||000003||Phil||12-03-1999||10:12 AM||||Yes the Formula was only made in '88  and was the least produced model all were v6 and yellow was the least produced color. So that would make it the "rarest" 88 although I believe the GT is the most sought after. If you are into collecting I suppose it would be worth looking into. There was a thread about finding a low/no mileage Fiero -would you drive it? Ah the problems we face.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||12-03-1999||05:45 PM||||Here I am talking about the FOCOA nationals in Columbus again.  I showed my Formula there, and about two cars down was a maroon Formula with only 1,800 miles on it.  It was beautiful.  The shifter knob still had all the little "bubbles" on it.  Original tires, everything.  The guy had been sent oversees so he put it in a "You Store It" place and picked it up just a couple years ago.  He was selling it for $14,000 I think. He said he drove it a couple hundred miles to the show, and then the same amount back. Very friendly guy, I must have talked/looked with him for over an hour.||||reg||1
